<?xml version="1.1" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog" xmlns:ext="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog-ext" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog-ext http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-ext.xsd http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-3.6.xsd">

    <!--
      Persist the light accent and the signal colour of the tenant seed set
      (ORISO-TenantService#154).

      The Admin theme builder has always submitted the full seed set
      { primaryColor, accent, secondaryColor, signal }, but only primaryColor and
      secondaryColor had columns, so the light accent ("Helle Akzentfarbe") and the
      signal colour were accepted with a 2xx and thrown away. theming_primary_color
      keeps its meaning unchanged (it is the DARK accent; other consumers depend on it)
      and theming_accent is its LIGHT counterpart. theming_signal is added in the same
      changeset so no field the Admin panel sends stays silently dropped.

      MIGRATION DECISION — deliberately NO backfill. Existing tenants get NULL, not a
      value derived from theming_primary_color. A derived colour written into the column
      would be indistinguishable from one an administrator actually chose, which is the
      exact failure mode this issue is about. NULL is the honest state "never configured";
      consumers derive their own light accent from primaryColor and must present it as
      derived. Both columns are therefore nullable, and no UPDATE runs here.

      varchar(15) matches the existing theming_primary_color / theming_secondary_color
      columns; the precondition marks the changeset ran where the columns already exist,
      so it is safe on fresh and on already-patched databases.
    -->
    <changeSet author="oriso" id="addThemingAccentAndSignal">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <columnExists tableName="tenant" columnName="theming_accent"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>
        <sqlFile path="db/changelog/changeset/0027_tenant_theming_accent_and_signal/addThemingAccentAndSignal.sql" stripComments="true" />
        <rollback>
            <sql>ALTER TABLE `tenantservice`.`tenant` DROP COLUMN `theming_accent`, DROP COLUMN `theming_signal`;</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
